Exercise: sa-storage-review (chapter 17 lab)

Work on serverb, with sudo or as root. Use the spare disk /dev/sdb (5 GiB,
empty). Do not touch /dev/sda.

Partitions
 1. A GPT table on /dev/sdb with three partitions:
      - about 1 GiB for project files,
      - about 1 GiB for backups,
      - about 512 MiB for swap.

File systems
 2. An XFS file system on the first partition, mounted on /srv/projects.
    Put a file /srv/projects/README.txt in it that contains the line
    "storage ready".
 3. An ext4 file system on the second partition, mounted on /srv/backups
    with the options noexec and nodev (plus the defaults).
 4. Swap space on the third partition.

Permanent
 5. All of it must come back after a reboot: fstab entries that identify the
    file systems and the swap area by UUID. Test with findmnt --verify and
    mount -a, and (recommended) with a real reboot.

On workstation
 6. Fill in answers.txt.

Then, on workstation:  lab grade sa-storage-review
